			Heading 1:
				Text: Letter from the President
			Paragraph: When we founded Solvent, eleven years ago, we had three rooftops, a borrowed windmill and more enthusiasm than money. Today we produce energy for more than eight thousand homes, shops and businesses in the county, and we do it without leaving it: what we generate here is consumed here.
				Style: lead
			Paragraph: 2025 has been the year of **consolidation**. We commissioned the Les Preses solar park, expanded the one at Sant Joan and repowered the three oldest wind turbines. We produced 11% more than the previous year and closed the year with a positive result for the fifth year in a row.
			Paragraph: None of this is the work of one person. It is the result of the work of the twenty-three people on our staff, of the more than twelve hundred members who make the decisions in the assembly, and of a network of local suppliers who have installed every kilowatt with their hands and with good judgment.
			Paragraph: This report tells what we have achieved, and also what it has cost us and what we still have to do. We invite you to read it with a critical eye: a cooperative improves by asking questions.
			Paragraph: With warm regards and eager to keep going,
			Text: Carme Vidal i Roca
